-# locals: policy (Hash tier => read groups, or nil)
-#
-# Read-only. A Work's per-file download limits are written from a collection's
-# or a set's Derivative access tab, so this shows them without offering an edit
-# that would be overwritten the next time that policy is applied.
- policy = (policy || {}).to_h.transform_keys(&:to_s)
- tiers = Sentinel::TIERS.select { |tier| policy.key?(tier) }
-# A bare section like its siblings on the Permissions tab, not a well: it is a
-# readout with nothing to submit, and a well reads as part of the form below.
.my-3
  %h5.pb-2 Download access by file
  %p.small.text-muted.mb-2
    Set from a collection's or a set's Derivative access tab, and changed there. A file not listed here
    follows this work's general permissions.
  - if tiers.empty?
    %p.small.mb-0 Every file follows this work's general permissions.
  - else
    %dl.row.mb-0.small
      - tiers.each do |tier|
        - groups = Array(policy[tier])
        %dt.col-sm-4.fw-semibold= tier_label(tier)
        %dd.col-sm-8.mb-1
          - if groups.empty?
            %span.text-muted Withheld from everyone
          - else
            = acl_grant_pills(groups.map { |g| g == 'public' ? 'Public' : pretty_group_name(g) })
